  "text": "# bko-holt load plan for layout.json\n# Source: ?, Sculpt OS, BIOS boot with sculpt, dumped 2026-11-08T02:54:28Z\n#\n# Disks:\n#   vdb (16 GiB) -> /dev/sdq\n#\n# Notes:\n#   - vdb2: the ESP, written as the source's with the partition table\n#   - Sculpt OS: load's log stays in the rescue system (its partition has no place for it)\n\n# ---- partition ----\n# vdb -> /dev/sdq: clear the old table and signatures\nwipefs --all /dev/sdq\n# vdb -> /dev/sdq: the source's table, GUIDs and boot code exactly\nsh -c 'bko-holt write-table layout.json vdb /dev/sdq $(blockdev --getsize64 /dev/sdq)'\n# the kernel reads the new table\npartx -u /dev/sdq\nudevadm settle\n\n# ---- assemble ----\n# (nothing to do)\n\n# ---- format ----\n# vdb3: ext2 \"GENODE\"\nmke2fs -F -q -t ext2 -O none,ext_attr,resize_inode,dir_index,filetype,sparse_super,large_file -U bc000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005 -L GENODE -b 4096 -I 256 -N 446464 -g 32768 -E hash_seed=bc000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006,resize=16777216 /dev/sdq3 16774420k\ntune2fs -r 209196 /dev/sdq3\n# check: /dev/sdq3 is ext2 with the source's features (read back by bko-holt's own probe)\n\n# ---- mount ----\nmkdir -p /mnt/bko-target\nmount -t ext2 -o defaults /dev/sdq3 /mnt/bko-target\n\n# ---- restore ----\n# snapshot latest of /srv/bko-repo, with BackOtter's restore flags\nRUSTIC_STRICT_EXIT=true rustic-bko --repository /srv/bko-repo --no-progress restore --numeric-id --glob '!/.bko-holt/system.json' --glob '!/.bko-holt' latest /mnt/bko-target\n\n# ---- boot ----\n# the boot code (MBR, freebsd-boot) was written with the partition table\n\n# ---- close ----\n# the restored tree\numount --recursive /mnt/bko-target\n\n# Nothing was written.  To run it: bko-holt load layout.json ... --through close --commit\n"
